  <!-- ── INDUSTRIES: SALONS, SPAS & AESTHETIC CLINICS ─────────────────── -->
  <section class="section fd-problem sol-industry">
    <div class="section__inner">
      <div class="section__header reveal">
        <h2 class="section__h2">Built for how each industry actually operates.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="sol-split reveal" id="salons">
        <div class="sol-split__img-col">
          <div class="fd-sscroll__img-wrap">
            <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560066984-138dadb4c035?w=800&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Stylist working with a client in a salon" class="fd-sscroll__img" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sol-split__text-col">
          <h3 class="fd-sscroll__title">Salons &amp; beauty studios</h3>
          <p class="sol-split__intro">A salon doesn&rsquo;t just schedule services &ndash; it schedules relationships. Zenly is built around how salon bookings actually work.</p>

          <div class="faq-list" x-data="{ open: null }">
            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 0 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 0 ? null : 0" :aria-expanded="open === 0">
                Scheduling that mirrors reality
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 0" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Every booking is created by staff and assigned to a specific stylist, moving through a clear lifecycle &ndash; Pending &rarr; Confirmed &rarr; In-Progress &rarr; Completed. Your team stops over-committing stylists, and clients get the stylist they came for, every time.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 1 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 1 ? null : 1" :aria-expanded="open === 1">
                Discount control across your chair count
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 1" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Staff can request a discount during booking, but it only applies once a manager approves it &ndash; every request carries a value and amount, so nothing&rsquo;s managed from memory. You stop losing margin to undocumented habit.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 2 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 2 ? null : 2" :aria-expanded="open === 2">
                Staff who move between branches
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 2" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Staff transfers are scheduled events, not informal arrangements &ndash; every move records the therapist, the destination branch, and the effective date. Your star stylists become a resource you share intelligently, not a liability you manage reactively.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sol-split reveal" id="spas" style="margin-top:var(--space-2xl);">
        <div class="sol-split__img-col">
          <div class="fd-sscroll__img-wrap">
            <img src="https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1663013569286-30b21b79a410?w=800&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Massage and spa treatment room" class="fd-sscroll__img" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sol-split__text-col">
          <h3 class="fd-sscroll__title">Spas &amp; wellness centers</h3>
          <p class="sol-split__intro">Spas are where operational imprecision is most expensive &ndash; every mistake fills the room, blocks the revenue, and damages the experience you&rsquo;ve spent years building.</p>

          <div class="faq-list" x-data="{ open: null }">
            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 0 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 0 ? null : 0" :aria-expanded="open === 0">
                Treatment-length precision
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 0" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Every booking carries a service ID &ndash; the treatment, its therapist, and its branch are all recorded from the moment a booking is created. Status updates tell every manager exactly when a room turns over, so your front desk stops guessing and clients stay in the experience you promised them.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 1 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 1 ? null : 1" :aria-expanded="open === 1">
                Protecting premium pricing
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 1" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Staff request discounts, managers approve &ndash; no approval, no discount. Every request shows the percentage and NPR value being surrendered, so your pricing strategy survives contact with the front desk.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 2 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 2 ? null : 2" :aria-expanded="open === 2">
                Specialist therapist availability
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 2" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Staff transfers are assigned to specific therapists with a destination branch and date, so managers across branches see incoming and outgoing specialist availability in advance &ndash; not on the day.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sol-split reveal" id="clinics" style="margin-top:var(--space-2xl);">
        <div class="sol-split__img-col">
          <div class="fd-sscroll__img-wrap">
            <img src="https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1677616799281-e1583ee2bdf0?w=800&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Aesthetic clinic treatment consultation" class="fd-sscroll__img" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sol-split__text-col">
          <h3 class="fd-sscroll__title">Aesthetic clinics &amp; medispas</h3>
          <p class="sol-split__intro">Aesthetic clinics run on trust. When a clinic runs on informal booking and manual payment reconciliation, it doesn&rsquo;t just create operational problems &ndash; it creates trust problems.</p>

          <div class="faq-list" x-data="{ open: null }">
            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 0 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 0 ? null : 0" :aria-expanded="open === 0">
                Consultation-to-treatment workflow
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 0" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Zenly&rsquo;s booking lifecycle &ndash; Pending, Confirmed, In-Progress, Completed &ndash; maps directly to a clinic&rsquo;s consultation-to-treatment flow, so managers see where every client is in their journey, at any branch, in real time.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 1 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 1 ? null : 1" :aria-expanded="open === 1">
                Payment precision without exceptions
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 1" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Every payment records the total amount and full settlement status at the point of service, so managers reconcile from a single source of truth &ndash; nothing settled from memory, nothing disputed from a WhatsApp exchange.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 2 }">
              <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 2 ? null : 2" :aria-expanded="open === 2">
                Discount control in a medical-pricing environment
                <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 2" x-cloak x-transition>
                <p>Discount requests are separated from discount decisions &ndash; clinic staff flag a discount, approval sits with the manager. Every approved discount shows the value and amount, creating an audit trail informal processes never provide.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ── SHARED CAPABILITIES ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__inner">
      <div class="section__header reveal">
        <h2 class="section__h2 section__h2--nowrap">Different businesses. One operational foundation.</h2>
        <p class="section__sub section__sub--center">Delivered across every industry on the platform.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fd-problem__grid fd-problem__grid--2col reveal" style="margin-top:var(--space-xl);">
        <div class="fd-problem__card">
          <h3 class="fd-problem__title">Multi-branch visibility</h3>
          <p class="fd-problem__text">Every branch, every booking, every status update &ndash; visible to the right role at the right level. Owners see the whole business. Managers see their branch. Staff see their day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fd-problem__card">
          <h3 class="fd-problem__title">Role-based access</h3>
          <p class="fd-problem__text">Admin, Manager, and Staff roles define who sees what and who can do what. You don&rsquo;t give your front desk the same access as your owner. Zenly doesn&rsquo;t either.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fd-problem__card">
          <h3 class="fd-problem__title">Real-time status tracking</h3>
          <p class="fd-problem__text">Bookings move from Pending to Confirmed to In-Progress to Completed. At any moment, every stakeholder knows what&rsquo;s happening across every branch without a phone call.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fd-problem__card">
          <h3 class="fd-problem__title">Complete payment records</h3>
          <p class="fd-problem__text">Every payment recorded at service time. Every amount logged. Every settlement tracked. Your financial picture is always current, always accurate, and always accessible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ── COMMON QUESTIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="faq">
    <div class="section__inner">
      <div class="faq-header reveal">
        <h2 class="section__h2">A few questions before you book a demo.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list" x-data="{ open: null }">
        <div class="faq-item reveal" data-delay="1" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 0 }">
          <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 0 ? null : 0" :aria-expanded="open === 0">
            My business doesn&rsquo;t fit neatly into salons, spas, or clinics.
            <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 0" x-cloak x-transition>
            <p>That&rsquo;s fine &ndash; the underlying system is the same for any appointment-based business with staff and branches. These three are just where we&rsquo;ve seen the clearest fit so far.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal" data-delay="2" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 1 }">
          <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 1 ? null : 1" :aria-expanded="open === 1">
            We only have one branch right now.
            <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 1" x-cloak x-transition>
            <p>Zenly works the same at one branch as it does at ten &ndash; you just won&rsquo;t need the multi-branch views yet. Most single-branch teams start for the booking and discount control alone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal" data-delay="3" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 2 }">
          <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 2 ? null : 2" :aria-expanded="open === 2">
            How is this different from generic booking software?
            <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 2" x-cloak x-transition>
            <p>Generic tools handle time slots. Zenly handles the operational reality underneath &ndash; stylist assignment, discount approvals, staff transfers, and payment reconciliation &ndash; because that&rsquo;s where service businesses actually lose money.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

